            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A new case of spontaneous pneumococcal peritonitis is described. The case is compared with the results of the literature. The absolute need to exclude a surgical aetiology before treating with adequate antibiotics is stressed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
